        "original_id": "a2291cb7-1a34-5d8f-b921-5e74aaf41b6b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Abraham Weinberg, George Weinberg, Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, Dutch Schultz, Jack \"Legs\" Diamond, Salvatore Maranzano\n- Roles: mobster, mob hitman, gunman, mob accountant\n- Places: New York City, Manhattan\n- Events: Manhattan Bootleg Wars, gangland slayings\n\nFacts:\n- During the 1920s and early 1930s, Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, born Uinseann Ó Colla on July 20, 1908, was an Irish American mob hitman in New York City.\n- During the 1920s and 1930s, George Weinberg was a New York mobster and, with his brother Abraham Weinberg, an associate of Dutch Schultz who worked as a mob accountant.\n- During the Manhattan Bootleg Wars, Abraham \"Abe\" Weinberg became one of Dutch Schultz's top gunmen.\n- Abraham \"Abe\" Weinberg was later a suspect in the gangland slayings of Jack \"Legs\" Diamond, Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, and Salvatore Maranzano.\n- George Weinberg was born in 1901 and died on January 29, 1939.\n- Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll died on February 7, 1932.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2601ca78-ef94-58a1-9e46-93489c476563",
        "text": "Page: Abraham Weinberg. Sentence: Abe Weinberg would become one of Schultz's top gunmen during the Manhattan Bootleg Wars and was a later suspect in the high-profile gangland slayings of Jack \"Legs\" Diamond, Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, and mob boss Salvatore Maranzano.\nPage: Mad Dog Coll. Sentence: Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll (born Uinseann Ó Colla, July 20, 1908 – February 7, 1932) was an Irish American mob hitman in the 1920s and early 1930s in New York City.\nPage: George Weinberg (mobster). Sentence: George Weinberg (1901 – January 29, 1939) was a New York mobster and, with brother Abraham Weinberg, an associate of Dutch Schultz as a mob accountant during the 1920s and 1930s.",
